23,2,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
24,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
25,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,The structural survey... it says the suspended bay has a weight limit. And the evening hires mean things are moving through the gallery often. I'm worried about things getting damaged or the floor not holding.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"My research indicates that static displays are less effective. Visitor numbers climb when there is a mechanism or a changing display, and people specifically value the presence of active staff or guides.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Rin,,"The conservation lab is a disaster! There's only one person working there and a huge pile of things waiting to be cleaned. Plus, most of our volunteers are just the town history group. Who's actually helping?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"I've found some real trouble! The paperwork for loans has been slipping past shipping deadlines, and the powered displays are breaking down constantly—some even during opening hours! We can't keep roping off the gallery.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears our budget is being quietly devoured by the logistics of movement. Transport and insurance for loans are consuming a staggering portion of our installation funds, and the cost of bespoke mounts is climbing rapidly.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Rin, if the lab is so backed up, maybe we shouldn't pick something that needs a lot of cleaning? I'm just... I'm really worried about the weight limits in the bay.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Kenji, if powered displays are failing, we must be cautious. However, the data shows that static, cased objects fail to draw repeat visitors. We need a balance between engagement and reliability.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Daisuke, you're right! We can't give that one poor person in the lab even more work. And @Toshio, if we need guides, we can't just rely on the history circle! We need real help!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Toshio, I agree we need engagement, but if the machines keep breaking, the visitors will just be looking at ""Out of Order"" signs! We have to find something that's exciting but actually works.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, a most poignant point. It would be a tragedy to curate a gallery of expensive signage. We must avoid any proposal that requires both complex machinery and bespoke mounting, lest we bankrupt the museum before the opening night.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree with Benjamin. And since the evening hires bring in caterers and chairs, we should avoid anything too fragile or spread out. It would be terrible if something broke because of the bookings.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, if the volunteer roster is limited, we should prioritize an exhibition that is easy to staff or provides its own expertise. We cannot afford a failure in visitor engagement.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, exactly! We can't just pretend we have a whole army of people. If the exhibition is too complicated to run, the few people we have left will just get super tired!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Daisuke, that's a great point about the caterers! If we combine fragile items with those shipping delays I found, we're just asking for a disaster. We need something sturdy and simple to get through the door!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are all dancing around the same conclusion. We require a selection that is structurally modest, mechanically simple, and—most importantly—logistically lean. I should hate for our budget to vanish into a void of crating fees and joiner's invoices.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I think we're all seeing the same risks. I just hope we can find something that doesn't put too much pressure on the building or the staff. I'm ready to see the candidates.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I agree. We must find a candidate that balances the need for dynamic engagement with the reality of our staffing and structural constraints. I am ready to review the proposals.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,4,talk,Rin,,I'm ready too! Let's find something that's super fun for the visitors but doesn't make the staff cry from too much work!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
43,2,4,pass,Rin,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
44,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm ready! Let's pick something that's a total hit with the crowd but actually arrives on time and stays working. I can't wait to see what we've got!,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,Indeed. Let us hope the candidates possess the grace to be both captivating and affordable. I am quite ready to see if any of them can survive our collective scrutiny.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
47,3,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
