50,3,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
51,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think Candidate A is the safest. The textiles are light, so they won't hurt the suspended bay, and they aren't as fragile as the other options when the caterers come through.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Candidate A is compelling. It provides the active presence of craftspeople that my data suggests visitors crave, while avoiding the mechanical failures Kenji noted and the weight issues Daisuke fears.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Rin,,"I love Candidate A! The craftspeople can help with the guiding, so the tired staff and the history circle don't have to do everything. Plus, it doesn't need the conservation lab to clean a million things!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Candidate A is awesome! It avoids the powered displays that keep breaking, and since the textiles are local, we won't have to worry about those shipping delays and paperwork nightmares I found!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Candidate A is a breath of fresh air. By utilizing local loans, we bypass the exorbitant transport costs and insurance fees that usually haunt our budget, and the lack of bespoke mounts should keep the joiner's invoices modest.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm just glad we all agree. Candidate B has too many loans, and C's conservation bench would put too much pressure on the lab. D is too risky with the rigging and the weight. A is... it's the most gentle choice.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"I concur. Candidate B relies on external loans that risk the shipping delays Kenji mentioned, and Candidate D's rigging is a liability for the suspended bay. A is the most stable and engaging option.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Daisuke, you're so right about Candidate C! Putting a conservation bench in the gallery is just mean to the one person left in the lab. They need a nap, not a crowd watching them work!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, exactly! And Candidate D is just a disaster waiting to happen with all those lights and motors. We'd be spending the whole season roping off the gallery for repairs! Candidate A is definitely the way to go.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Daisuke, your caution is well-placed. Candidate B would be a logistical nightmare of crating fees, and Candidate D's overhead rigging sounds like a recipe for both structural anxiety and budget depletion. Candidate A is simply the most rational path.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I feel much better now that we've talked it through. I'm happy to vote for Candidate A. It's the only one that doesn't make me worry about the building or the people.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"I agree. Candidate A aligns with the visitor data by offering a dynamic experience, while remaining the most resilient against our operational and structural weaknesses. I vote for Candidate A.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Rin,,I'm voting for Candidate A too! It's the only one that's actually fair to the staff and doesn't make the lab person do a million things. It's a win-win for everyone!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"I'm voting for Candidate A! It's the only one that doesn't feel like a gamble. No shipping delays, no broken motors, and it'll actually be open for the visitors to enjoy!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,I shall join the chorus. Candidate A is the only proposal that doesn't treat our budget as a bottomless pit or our staff as martyrs. It is logically the most sustainable choice. I vote for Candidate A.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
